َخَلْتُم بُيُوتًا فَسَلِّمُوا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِكُمْ تَحِيَّةً مِّنْ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ مُبَـٰرَكَةً طَيِّبَةً ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمُ ٱلْـَٔايَـٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"No blame will be attached to the blind, the lame, the sick.Whether you eat in your own houses, or those of your fathers, your mothers, your brothers, your sisters, your paternal uncles, your paternal aunts, your maternal uncles, your maternal aunts, houses you have the keys for, or any of your friends’ houses, you will not be blamed: you will not be blamed whether you eat in company or separately. When you enter any house, greet one another with a greeting of blessing and goodness as enjoined by God. This is how God makes His messages clear to you so that you may understand.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"لَّيْسَ","en_gloss":"Not is","transliteration":"laysa","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":2,"ar":"عَلَى","en_gloss":"on","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلْأَعْمَىٰ","en_gloss":"the blind","transliteration":"l-aʿmā","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":4,"ar":"حَرَجٌۭ","en_gloss":"any blame","transliteration":"ḥarajun","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":5,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"and not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":6,"ar":"عَلَى","en_gloss":"on","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ٱلْأَعْرَجِ","en_gloss":"the lame","transliteration":"l-aʿraji","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":8,"ar":"حَرَجٌۭ","en_gloss":"any blame","transliteration":"ḥarajun","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"and not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":10,"ar":"عَلَى","en_gloss":"on","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱلْمَرِيضِ","en_gloss":"the sick","transliteration":"l-marīḍi","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":12,"ar":"حَرَجٌۭ","en_gloss":"any blame","transliteration":"ḥarajun","verse_key":"24:61"},{"pos":13,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"and not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"24:61"}